{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "t13-leash-child-fifty-parent-ninety-env-does-not-reach-child",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 14 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 10/L10): LOHRA_MAX_ITERATIONS=3 bounds only the PARENT's own leash (the parent itself needs exactly 3: spawn_session, collect_session, final text) — a spawned child, needing 4 iterations to complete (three tool_calls round trips, then a final text), is NOT bound by the env override at all and completes successfully, since its own fixed leash (50, decision 10) is far above 4. If the env value had leaked into the child's own leash, iteration 4 would never be reached and the turn would fail with MaxIterationsError instead. Kept cheap deliberately: the child only needs to cross the env's low ceiling by one, not approach its own real ceiling (50).",
  "argv": [
    "chat",
    "SCEN:parent spawn a child needing four iterations",
    "--json",
    "--provider",
    "ollama",
    "--model",
    "stub-coder:1b"
